<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Entities Pane</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Entities pane is located in the left hand side of the KUBE window. Entities pane is a powerful tool, which allows the user to work quickly on all data entities in a document, without having to select them in the window. This pane allows you to manage your data and the way it is displayed.</p>
<p>Entities pane contains a <u style="text-decoration:none;"><a href="Tree.htm">tree</a></u> structure of the data stored in the document. If several documents are open, Entities pane shows the data structure of the active one. Root of the tree is the filename. All entities are grouped by type. Second level of the tree consists of the available types in the document. The lowest level consists of the entities themselves.</p>
<p><img src="Images/entities_pane.gif" width="364px" height="304px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>For example, all mesh entities derive from Meshes group, all datum entities derive from Datuming group, <span lang="EN-US">etc.</span> with the exception of the datum points generated by importing ASCII file as individual entities – in this case points derive from Datum Points group<span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
<p>Entity operations are mainly performed using the <u style="text-decoration:none;"><a href="Tree_Context_Menus.htm">tree context menus</a></u> (right click mouse button). The context menu will change depending on the entity type.</p>
